From: Hermes Agent
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: dtc: fix multiple definition of yylloc with bison 3.x

dtc 1.4.5's flex lexer (dtc-lexer.l) defines YYLTYPE yylloc, while bison
3.x generates its own definition of yylloc in dtc-parser.tab.c (declared
extern in dtc-parser.tab.h, which dtc-lexer.l already includes). Both
translation units define yylloc, so linking dtc fails with:

    multiple definition of 'yylloc'
    collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status

Remove the duplicate definition from the lexer so the single definition
generated by bison is used. The lexer sees the extern declaration via
dtc-parser.tab.h.

Signed-off-by: Hermes Agent <hermes@nousresearch.com>
---
 dtc-lexer.l | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dtc-lexer.l b/dtc-lexer.l
index 4d4c6b2..e2b5a1a 100644
--- a/dtc-lexer.l
+++ b/dtc-lexer.l
@@ -38,7 +38,6 @@
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
 extern bool treesource_error;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
